Package: totaljs-docker-stack
Version: 1.0.0-1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Total.js <repository@totaljs.com>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: totaljs-docker-source (>= 1.0.0), docker-ce, docker-ce-cli, containerd.io, docker-buildx-plugin, docker-compose-plugin
Homepage: https://www.totaljs.com
Description: Docker and the services of the Total.js Developer Distros
 Docker Engine with its Compose plugin, and the services that a Total.js developer
 uses, as editable Compose files in /www: a reverse proxy (nginx-proxy), Total.js Code,
 Total.js Flow, and PostgreSQL with pgAdmin. Each one is a systemd service
 (totaljs-proxy, totaljs-code, totaljs-flow, totaljs-postgres) that starts at boot
 and downloads its images the first time it starts, not while the package is installed.
 The files are copied to /www only if they are not there, so what the person edits is
 never overwritten by an update.
